==English==

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{inh|en|enm|charlet}}, {{m|enm|charlette||dish made from eggs, meat, milk, etc.}}, probably from {{der|en|fro|[[char]] [[laitée]]||meat with milk}}<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=charlet(te, n.|id=MED7275|accessdate=19 June 2018|nodot=yes}}; see {{cite-book|author=A[bram] Smythe Palmer|authorlink=Abram Smythe Palmer|chapter={{smallcaps|Charlotte}}|title=Folk-etymology: A Dictionary of Verbal Corruptions or Words Perverted in Form or Meaning, by False Derivation or Mistaken Analogy|location=London|publisher=[[w:George Bell & Sons|George Bell and Sons]],{{nb...|York Street, Covent Garden}}|year=1882|page=59|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/cu31924027422405#page/n90/mode/1up|column=2|oclc=23927813}}.</ref> (see {{cog|fr|charlotte}} below); or borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|charlotte}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈʃɑːlət/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈʃɑɹlət/|lang=en}}
